NAME
    wmview - image viewer WM client (Path C phase 42)

SYNOPSIS
    wmview PATH [SECONDS]

DESCRIPTION
    Open a 400x300 window and display the contents of the
    binary-PPM (P6) image at PATH.  Images larger than the
    content area (400 wide, ~278 tall after title bar) are
    clipped; smaller images are centered against a dark
    background.  SECONDS is the lifetime cap (default 600 =
    10 minutes); Ctrl-Q exits early.

    The image is decoded once at startup and blitted directly
    into the window's shared pixel surface — no per-pixel
    syscall overhead.  Subsequent frames only repaint the
    title bar so focus changes track correctly.

    Format requirements:
      - P6 magic ("P6" + whitespace, NOT the ASCII P3 variant)
      - maxval 255 (8-bit RGB)
      - '#'-prefixed comment lines allowed in the header

    A test image ships at /sample.ppm — a 64x48 four-colour
    quadrant tile with a diagonal brightness gradient.  Run:

        wmview /sample.ppm

    to verify the viewer is working.

LIMITATIONS
    No scaling — images larger than the window are clipped at
    the top-left of the content area.  No PNG/JPEG/BMP support;
    P6 PPM only.  No animation, no zoom, no save.  Single
    256 KiB scratch buffer caps the largest file at ~256x256x4
    with header overhead.

SEE ALSO
    wmpaint(1) draws PPM-style content procedurally.  wmd(1)
    runs the WM that hosts this client.
